## Behaviour and content

Each section has a short, meaningful heading. The enhanced GOV.UK component supplies its own expand and collapse buttons and a show-all control. Its unenhanced HTML leaves the content readable. Do not replace its button with a clickable heading or manage a second, competing open state.

Opening a section must not trigger a device command, reload data or discard a pending form. Use the same labels in search results and related links so the topic is easy to find. Keep explanations short enough to compare across sections.

## Accessibility and testing

Tab to each control, toggle it with Enter and Space, then inspect its expanded state with a screen reader. Confirm that focus stays on the triggering button. Test all-open content at 320px and 200% text size. With JavaScript disabled, verify every section remains present and in a logical heading order.

## Home Assistant boundary

This is a reference for custom help content. It does not convert native Home Assistant expansion panels or persist their state. Reuse native panels where they already meet the task, and test their actual labels and focus separately.

